The orientation core in Sources/TEMCore/SEM/Orientation/ (RotationConversions, Rotation, PointGroup, OrientationRegion,
Orientations, Misorientations, OrientationSampling) is a port of orix 0.15.0's orix.quaternion package (_conversions,
quaternion, rotation, symmetry, orientation_region, misorientation, orientation, _numba) and of orix.sampling
(sample_generators, _cubochoric_sampling), Copyright (C) 2018-2026 the orix developers,
GPL-3.0-or-later, taken under GPL-3.0; the conversions follow Rowenhorst et al. (2015), Modelling Simul. Mater. Sci. Eng.
23 083501. Its parity inputs, tools/parity/sem/fixtures/orientation_inputs.json, hold seeded rotations and the Bunge
angles of the first 2000 rows of orix-data's Ti_orientations.ctf (CC BY 4.0).

The vectors, projections and colour keys beside it (SphericalVectors, Miller, FundamentalSector, ColorKeys) port orix
0.15.0's orix.vector (vector3d, miller, fundamental_sector, spherical_region), orix.projections.stereographic,
orix.plot.direction_color_keys and orix.plot.orientation_color_keys, and the lattice alignment of
orix.crystal_map._phase, same copyright and licence; the TSL key follows MTEX (GPL-2.0-or-later, as orix states) and
Nolze & Hielscher (2016), J. Appl. Cryst. 49, 1786. The HSV conversion is matplotlib's hsv_to_rgb (PSF-style licence).

The map pictures of the Maps room (Sources/TEMCore/SEM/CrystalMap/OrientationMaps.swift) follow orix 0.15.0's
CrystalMap.plot and get_map_data with its IPF colour keys, same copyright and licence.

The crystal map model in Sources/TEMCore/SEM/CrystalMap/ (CrystalMap, PhaseList, CrystalPhase, NeighbourMisorientation)
