MTEX code is used. Figure F13 is computed on orix-data's Ti_orientations.ctf (CC BY 4.0).

The grain analysis in Sources/TEMCore/SEM/Grains/ (GrainMap, DefDAPSymmetry, GrainBoundaries, GrainSegmentation,
KernelAverageMisorientation, GrainOrientationStatistics) is a port of DefDAP 1.3.1 (https://github.com/MechMicroMan/DefDAP):
defdap.ebsd (find_boundaries, find_grains, build_neighbour_network, calc_kam, Grain.calc_average_ori,
build_mis_ori_list, calc_grod), defdap._accelerated (flood_fill), defdap.quat (create_many_quats, calc_sym_eqvs,
calc_average_ori, calcMisOri) and the symmetry tables of defdap.crystal. Copyright 2025 Mechanics of Microstructures
Group at The University of Manchester. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0), which is compatible with GPL-3.0; DefDAP ships no NOTICE file. Changes:
rewritten in Swift; boundaries take the symmetry of each pair's phase where DefDAP takes the primary phase's; a
symmetric KAM with a threshold is added beside DefDAP's (kept as KernelAverageMisorientation.Method.defdap); the GOS is
the mean GROD angle beside DefDAP's mean cosine. Its parity input tools/parity/sem/fixtures/grain_inputs.json holds rows
0-89, columns 0-119 of orix-data's Ti_orientations.ctf (CC BY 4.0).

