DefDAP (ported code and data)
================================================================================

The slip analysis in Sources/TEMCore/SEM/Deformation/ (DefDAPQuat, DefDAPCrystalStructure, SlipSystem, SlipSystemSet,
SlipPhase, SlipTraceAnalysis, NyeTensor) is a port of DefDAP 1.3.1 (https://github.com/MechMicroMan/DefDAP): defdap.quat,
defdap.crystal, defdap.crystal_utils and defdap.ebsd (calc_nye, calc_average_ori, calc_average_schmid_factors,
calc_slip_traces), and SlipSystems.swift carries DefDAP's slip-system files (defdap/slip_systems/*.txt) verbatim.
Copyright 2025 Mechanics of Microstructures Group at The University of Manchester. Licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0), which is compatible with GPL-3.0; DefDAP ships no NOTICE file.
Changes: DefDAP's Python is rewritten in Swift; NyeTensor keeps the x and y derivatives apart by default where DefDAP 1.3.1
aliases them (its numbers remain available); SlipPhase.analysisSlipSystems drops twelve rows of cubic_bcc whose slip
direction is not in its plane. The parity inputs tools/parity/sem/fixtures/slip_inputs.json hold rows 0-89, columns
0-119 of orix-data's Ti_orientations.ctf and the whole sdss_ferrite_austenite.ang (both CC BY 4.0).

