================================================================================
Demo data shipped in the app (Contents/Resources/DemoData/)
================================================================================

Four public datasets ship in the application bundle unchanged, so that anyone can try the SEM rooms without a microscope file
(Help > Open Demo Data, the welcome window's Try Demo Data). Each is the copy its source publishes; the repository's
DemoData/ folder holds them and `DemoDocuments.Shipped` pins their size and md5.

nickel_ebsd_large/patterns_v2.h5 (15,368,325 bytes, md5 51d6bc0f5ff23dcb0c1a8e1f4c52d4d4)
    4125 electron backscatter diffraction patterns (55 x 75 scan, 60 x 60 pixels, 8 bit) from polycrystalline nickel, acquired
    on a NORDIF UF-1100 detector at 20 kV and 70° tilt, with the static background, the projection centres and an orix
    crystal map. From the kikuchipy data repository https://github.com/pyxem/kikuchipy-data (commit
    bcab8f7a4ffdb86a97f14e2327a4813d3156a85e, the file kikuchipy 0.13's `data.nickel_ebsd_large()` fetches), part of
    H. W. Ånes, J. Hjelen, A. T. J. van Helvoort and K. Marthinsen, "Electron backscatter patterns from Nickel acquired with
    varying camera gain" [Data set], Zenodo, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7498632. Licensed under the Creative Commons
    Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/); text in
    `Licenses/kikuchipy-data-nickel_ebsd_large-LICENSE.txt`.

EDS_SEM_TM002.hspy (31,008 bytes, md5 1c3b8fddb2698741a0948d5a7c4eec51)
    One SEM-EDS spectrum of the EDS-TM002 standard of the Bundesanstalt für Materialforschung und -prüfung (BAM): a layer of
    about 6 µm holding C, Al, Mn, Cu and Zr on a silicon substrate, acquired on a Carl Zeiss Nvision40 with an Oxford
    Instruments X-max 80 detector at 10 kV (1024 channels of 10 eV from -100 eV; live time 20.0 s). The file is
    `exspy/data/EDS_SEM_TM002.hspy` of the eXSpy package (https://github.com/hyperspy/exspy), Copyright 2007-2026 The eXSpy
    developers, GPL-3.0-or-later (text in LICENSE, which is version 3 of the same licence). macTEM reads the spectrum with its
    own reader of HyperSpy's HDF5 layout (`HyperSpySpectrumFile`); no eXSpy or RosettaSciIO code is copied.

ni_mc_mp_20kv_uint8_gzip_opts9.h5 (908,492 bytes, md5 807c8306a0d02b46effbcb12bd44cd02)
    The dynamically simulated EBSD master pattern of nickel at 20 kV (EMsoft EMMCOpenCL and EMEBSDmaster), 401 x 401 pixels
    in the square Lambert and the stereographic projection of both hemispheres, reduced to 8 bit with gzip by kikuchipy. The
    file is `kikuchipy/data/emsoft_ebsd_master_pattern/ni_mc_mp_20kv_uint8_gzip_opts9.h5` of kikuchipy 0.13.1
    (https://github.com/pyxem/kikuchipy, the file `data.nickel_ebsd_master_pattern_small()` loads), Copyright 2019-2026 the
    kikuchipy developers, GPL-3.0-or-later; the master pattern itself is H. W. Ånes, "EBSD master pattern of nickel at
    20 kV" [Data set], Zenodo, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7498645, CC BY 4.0 (text in
    `Licenses/kikuchipy-data-nickel_ebsd_large-LICENSE.txt`, the same licence). macTEM reads it with its own reader
    (`EMsoftMasterPatternReader`).

sdss_ferrite_austenite.ang (651,687 bytes, md5 0c45548b82445657fbd52d882a27f2fd)
    An EBSD orientation map of a super duplex stainless steel, 100 x 117 points at 1.5 µm, two phases (austenite and
    ferrite) with dot product and image quality, indexed with EMsoft; EBSD data by Jarle Hjelen, NTNU. The file is
    `sdss_ferrite_austenite.ang` of the orix data repository https://github.com/pyxem/orix-data (the file orix 0.15's
    `data.sdss_ferrite_austenite()` fetches; doi:10.5281/zenodo.3625780), licensed under CC BY 4.0 (text in
    `Licenses/orix-data-sdss_ferrite_austenite-LICENSE.txt`). macTEM reads it with its own port of orix's .ang reader.

